HiBreak Pro Color: incoming VoLTE calls without +EAIC approval.

Applied by build-hibreak.py to the smali of TrebleDroid's com.mediatek.ims
(ims-mtk-u-resigned.apk, versionName 13), decoded with apktool 3.0.3
`d -r`. See MTK-VOLTE.md.

rw-system.sh rewrites AT+EAIC=2 to AT+EAIC=3 in the vendor RIL, so the
modem no longer asks for incoming call approval and sends no +EAIC. An
incoming VoLTE call then arrives only as +ECPI <id>,0 (call mode >= 20),
which the stock service drops because no session exists yet.

- HbpcMtEcpiHandler (new): one extra call-info listener per phone,
  registered next to registerForCallAdditionalInfo in ImsService.<init>
  and notifyMultiSimConfigChanged; forwards every indication to
  ImsService.hbpcOnMtEcpi. android.os.Registrant holds its Handler only
  weakly, so a static list keeps a strong reference to each listener.
- ImsService.hbpcOnMtEcpi (new): for ECPI 0 with a call id, call mode
  >= 20 and a valid phone id, skip the call if an MT for that id is
  pending (mPendingMTCallId) or a session already tracks it. Otherwise
  do what sendIncomingCallIndication and setCallIndicationInternal do:
  clear mIsPendingMTTerminated, set mPendingMTCallId, register the
  service handler for call info (EVENT 8, so an early 133 marks the
  pending MT terminated), build the MT call profile, and post EVENT 27
  marked hbpcNoApproval.
- ImsService$MyHandler case 27: with hbpcNoApproval, skip
  setCallIndication (AT+EAIC=0), hand the ECPI to the new session and
  clear the pending call id (ImsService.hbpcMtSessionCreated), so a later
  call that reuses the id is not skipped. The stock handling of a
  pending 133 then runs as usual.
- ImsCallSessionProxy.hbpcDeliverCallInfo (new): replay the ECPI as
  EVENT_CALL_INFO_INDICATION, so the stock code reports the incoming
  call.

Info-level logs under the ImsService tag: listener registration, every
call-info indication (phone id, call id, message type, call mode; no
number) and each skip.

